//
// A NULLABLE NARROW ARGUMENT INTO A DENSE MEMBER IS REFUSED (`@FR-Disp-Specific` crossed with
// `@FR-N-Store`).  `u8? → u8` ranks LOSSY and is the only applicable member of `(u8 | text)`, but
// N-Store makes storing a `u8?` into a `u8` slot a hard ERROR — a narrow width's null sentinel is a
// valid `u8` — so the selection does not license the store: the call is refused at compile time,
// naming the discharge.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; refused as the rule says, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the parameter and the cure.
// HOLDS: `a-nullable-argument-reaches-a-dense-member-only-as-the-lossy-rank` (the wide widths warn).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: a nullable `u8?` cannot be stored into parameter 1 of `s5`

fn s5(x: u8) -> text { "u8 {x}" }
fn s5(t: text) -> text { "text {t}" }

fn main() {
  u: u8? = 4;
  println(s5(u));
}
